IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ap-dates`
IMPORT `ap-duties`
IMPORT `ap-family-provision`
IMPORT `ap-seat`

-- Administration and Probate Act 1958 (Vic), Part IV -- worked cases for the claimant's family provision questions
-- (ap-seat.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output.
-- Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases: Part IV`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`

-- The death in most cases: 1 June 2026. A date for "any day": 1 January 2000.
`D` MEANS `d` 1 6 2026
`any day` MEANS `d` 1 1 2000

§§ `s 90 -- am I an eligible person`

-- Arguments: relationship, day of death, registered, living together, years together, parent of a child under 18, age,
-- student, impairment, permanent, reduced capacity, participation affected, could have taken FLA proceedings, not taken or
-- finalised, prevented by death, child has died, day child died, household member, past household member likely to return.
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `the deceased's spouse at the death` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `paragraph (a): the spouse or domestic partner at the death`
-- Domestic partners (s 3): 2 years together, or a child under 18 together, or registered.
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `living with the deceased as a couple, or a registered domestic partner` `D` FALSE TRUE 2 FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `paragraph (a): the spouse or domestic partner at the death`
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `living with the deceased as a couple, or a registered domestic partner` `D` FALSE TRUE 1.9 FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not an eligible person`
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `living with the deceased as a couple, or a registered domestic partner` `D` FALSE TRUE 1 TRUE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `paragraph (a): the spouse or domestic partner at the death`
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `living with the deceased as a couple, or a registered domestic partner` `D` TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `paragraph (a): the spouse or domestic partner at the death`
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `living with the deceased as a couple, or a registered domestic partner` `D` FALSE TRUE 1 FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `paragraph (k): a member of the deceased's household`
-- Children: under 18; full-time student 18 to 25 (both ends, fork F8); 26; an adult child; a disability (all four limbs).
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `the deceased's child, including an adopted child` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 17 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `paragraph (b): a child under 18, a full-time student aged 18 to 25, or a child with a disability`
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `the deceased's child, including an adopted child` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 18 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `paragraph (b): a child under 18, a full-time student aged 18 to 25, or a child with a disability`
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `the deceased's child, including an adopted child` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 25 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `paragraph (b): a child under 18, a full-time student aged 18 to 25, or a child with a disability`
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `the deceased's child, including an adopted child` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 26 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `paragraph (f): any other child or stepchild`
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `the deceased's child, including an adopted child` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 18 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `paragraph (f): any other child or stepchild`
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `the deceased's child, including an adopted child` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 40 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `paragraph (b): a child under 18, a full-time student aged 18 to 25, or a child with a disability`
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `the deceased's child, including an adopted child` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 40 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `paragraph (f): any other child or stepchild`
-- Stepchildren and those treated as natural children.
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `the deceased's stepchild` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 17 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `paragraph (c): a stepchild under 18, a full-time student aged 18 to 25, or with a disability`
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `the deceased's stepchild` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `paragraph (f): any other child or stepchild`
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `a person who believed the deceased was their parent and was treated as the deceased's natural child` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 20 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `paragraph (d): a person treated as a natural child, under 18, a full-time student aged 18 to 25, or with a disability`
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `a person who believed the deceased was their parent and was treated as the deceased's natural child` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `paragraph (g): any other person treated as a natural child`
-- Former partners: all three limbs of (e), or not.
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `the deceased's former spouse or former domestic partner` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `paragraph (e): a former spouse or domestic partner prevented by the death from Family Law Act proceedings`
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `the deceased's former spouse or former domestic partner` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not an eligible person`
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `the deceased's former spouse or former domestic partner` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `any day` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `paragraph (k): a member of the deceased's household`
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `the deceased's registered caring partner` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `paragraph (h): a registered caring partner`
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `the deceased's grandchild` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `paragraph (i): a grandchild`
-- A child's partner: the child died on 1 June 2027 (exactly a year after, fork F9), 2 June 2027, or the day before the death.
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `the spouse or domestic partner of the deceased's child` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 6 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `paragraph (j): the spouse or domestic partner of a child who died within one year of the deceased`
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `the spouse or domestic partner of the deceased's child` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 2 6 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not an eligible person`
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `the spouse or domestic partner of the deceased's child` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 31 5 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not an eligible person`
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `the spouse or domestic partner of the deceased's child` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not an eligible person`
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `the spouse or domestic partner of the deceased's child` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 2 6 2027) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `paragraph (k): a member of the deceased's household`
-- No listed relationship: a household member, past or present, or no one.
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `none of these` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `paragraph (k): a member of the deceased's household`
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `none of these` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `paragraph (k): a member of the deceased's household`
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person` `none of these` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not an eligible person`

§§ `ss 90A, 91, 101 -- may the Court make an order`

-- ... then dependent, moral duty, inadequate provision, in time.
#ASSERT `Can the Court make a family provision order for me` `the deceased's spouse at the death` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Court make a family provision order for me` `the deceased's spouse at the death` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court make a family provision order for me` `the deceased's spouse at the death` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court make a family provision order for me` `the deceased's spouse at the death` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Paragraphs (h) to (k) need dependency (s 91(2)(b)).
#ASSERT `Can the Court make a family provision order for me` `the deceased's grandchild` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court make a family provision order for me` `the deceased's grandchild` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Court make a family provision order for me` `none of these` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Court make a family provision order for me` `none of these` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An adult child (paragraph (f)) need not show dependency.
#ASSERT `Can the Court make a family provision order for me` `the deceased's child, including an adopted child` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 45 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 101: a death before 1 January 2015 is left to Part IV as it was.
#ASSERT `Can the Court make a family provision order for me` `the deceased's spouse at the death` (`d` 31 12 2014) FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the Court make a family provision order for me` `the deceased's spouse at the death` (`d` 1 1 2015) FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 91(4), (5) -- what the Court must weigh`

#ASSERT `What must the Court weigh in fixing my provision` `the deceased's spouse at the death` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS (LIST `the degree of the deceased's moral duty to provide for me (s 91(4)(a))`, `the degree to which the estate fails to provide adequately for me (s 91(4)(b))`, `no more than is necessary for my proper maintenance and support (s 91(5)(a))`)
#ASSERT `What must the Court weigh in fixing my provision` `the deceased's child, including an adopted child` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS (LIST `the degree of the deceased's moral duty to provide for me (s 91(4)(a))`, `the degree to which the estate fails to provide adequately for me (s 91(4)(b))`, `the degree to which I cannot provide adequately for myself by reasonable means (s 91(4)(c))`, `no more than is necessary for my proper maintenance and support (s 91(5)(a))`)
#ASSERT `What must the Court weigh in fixing my provision` `the deceased's grandchild` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS (LIST `the degree of the deceased's moral duty to provide for me (s 91(4)(a))`, `the degree to which the estate fails to provide adequately for me (s 91(4)(b))`, `the degree of my dependency on the deceased at the death (s 91(4)(d))`, `no more than is necessary for my proper maintenance and support (s 91(5)(a))`, `proportionate to my degree of dependency on the deceased at the death (s 91(5)(b))`)
#ASSERT `What must the Court weigh in fixing my provision` `none of these` `D` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS EMPTY

§§ `s 99 -- time to apply`

#ASSERT `By when must I apply for family provision` (`d` 15 3 2027) EQUALS `d` 15 9 2027
#ASSERT `By when must I apply for family provision` (`d` 31 8 2027) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2028
#ASSERT `By when must I apply for family provision` (`d` 31 3 2027) EQUALS `d` 30 9 2027

-- Arguments: day of the grant, applied, day applied, today, Court extended, finally distributed first. Grant 15 March 2027;
-- last day 15 September 2027.
#ASSERT `Where does my family provision application stand` (`d` 15 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 15 9 2027) (`d` 1 10 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Where does my family provision application stand` (`d` 15 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 16 9 2027) (`d` 1 10 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `late: it can go ahead only if the Court extends the period`
#ASSERT `Where does my family provision application stand` (`d` 15 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 16 9 2027) (`d` 1 10 2027) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `late, but the Court has extended the period`
#ASSERT `Where does my family provision application stand` (`d` 15 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 16 9 2027) (`d` 1 10 2027) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `late, and the period can no longer be extended, as the estate has been finally distributed`
#ASSERT `Where does my family provision application stand` (`d` 15 3 2027) FALSE `any day` (`d` 15 9 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `still open: apply by the last day`
#ASSERT `Where does my family provision application stand` (`d` 15 3 2027) FALSE `any day` (`d` 16 9 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `late: it can go ahead only if the Court extends the period`

§§ `s 99A -- distributions`

#ASSERT `When does my notice of intention lapse` (`d` 10 1 2027) EQUALS `d` 10 4 2027
#ASSERT `When does my notice of intention lapse` (`d` 30 11 2026) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2027

-- Arguments: properly made, for maintenance of partner or dependent child, I consented in writing, day of the grant, day of
-- distribution, notice of an application, notice of intention given, day notice received, applied, day applied, written
-- notice of application received. Grant 1 January 2027; six months run to 1 July 2027.
#ASSERT `Can I proceed against the executor over a distribution` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2027) (`d` 2 7 2027) FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I proceed against the executor over a distribution` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2027) (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I proceed against the executor over a distribution` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 1 2027) (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I proceed against the executor over a distribution` TRUE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2027) (`d` 2 7 2027) FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I proceed against the executor over a distribution` TRUE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2027) (`d` 1 7 2027) FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I proceed against the executor over a distribution` TRUE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2027) (`d` 2 7 2027) TRUE FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A notice of intention received 1 March 2027 lapses after 1 June 2027 unless an application is made by then.
#ASSERT `Can I proceed against the executor over a distribution` TRUE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2027) (`d` 2 7 2027) TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2027) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I proceed against the executor over a distribution` TRUE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2027) (`d` 2 7 2027) TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 2 6 2027) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I proceed against the executor over a distribution` TRUE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2027) (`d` 2 7 2027) TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
